                <pb facs="0545" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.51632 National City Bank/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-28T12:00:00-03:00">February 28,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received February 28—11:20 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>5. Department’s telegram No. 6, February 27, 7 p.m. Facts reported through the
                    Department by bank substantially correct and matter has been in conference
                    between local branch authorities and Embassy for some time.</p>
                <p>Will use influence with Foreign Office to obtain postponement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
